{:edb/db-before-t 1370 :edb/db-after-t 1371 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534683 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:06:34.886Z" 13194139534683 true] [17592186184132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303228 13194139534683 true] [17592186184132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303242 13194139534683 true] [17592186184133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303221 13194139534683 true] [17592186184133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303235 13194139534683 true] [17592186184133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303249 13194139534683 true] [17592186303221 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303222 13194139534683 true] [17592186303221 1089 "q-112625" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303221 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534683 true] [17592186303221 1100 "The equation $-4{w}^{2}-16w+9=0$ can be written in the form $4(w+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p,$ and solve the equation." 13194139534683 true] [17592186303221 1113 #uuid "81d5e8dd-0fd3-5d41-bcce-bd1a45fe46d8" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303221 1145 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{w}^{2}-16w+9) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}+16w-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{w}^{2}+16w-9 & =0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}+16w & =9 \\\\ 4({w}^{2}+4w) & =9 \\\\ 4[{w}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot w+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}] & =9 \\\\ 4[{(w+2)}^{2}-4] & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w+2)}^{2}-4\\cdot 4 & =9 \\\\ 4{(w+2)}^{2}-16 & =9 \\\\ 4{(w+2)}^{2} & =9+16 \\\\ 4{(w+2)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=2.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w+2)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {(w+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(w+2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\ |w+2| & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ w+2 & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ w & =-2\\pm \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =-2-\\frac{5}{2}=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ w & =-2+\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $w=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303223 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303224 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303225 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303226 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303227 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1041 "selection" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303227 13194139534683 true] [17592186303222 1110 #uuid "bcc75e1d-788b-5862-9a3a-03638dd85835" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303223 1034 "$p=1,\\,w=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $w=1$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534683 true] [17592186303223 1111 #uuid "94a0b787-6dd0-5672-9d6c-d9eeb327b09c" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303224 1034 "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{5}{2}$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534683 true] [17592186303224 1111 #uuid "f87ad25e-6551-5ae9-bfb7-a51eb3a4b147" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303225 1034 "$p=1,\\,w=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534683 true] [17592186303225 1111 #uuid "1c14e08a-d55a-58f3-98b9-30e648738da2" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303226 1034 "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{3}{2}$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534683 true] [17592186303226 1111 #uuid "2b1c8c06-9fb1-501a-8f08-cdd2363e9d25" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303227 1034 "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534683 true] [17592186303227 1111 #uuid "5ff954d1-2a48-549d-bf7b-5c715ddf3c1e" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303228 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303229 13194139534683 true] [17592