factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x & =-41 \\\\ 20({x}^{2}-3x) & =-41 \\\\ 20[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}] & =-41 \\\\ 20[{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}] & =-41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-20\\cdot \\frac{9}{4} & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-45 & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =45-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=4.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{20} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{2}| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303237 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303238 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303239 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303240 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303241 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1041 "selection" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303239 13194139534683 true] [17592186303236 1110 #uuid "04ca9809-ed2f-5683-825b-a4a7f232695a" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303237 1034 "q=4,\\,x=2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534683 true] [17592186303237 1111 #uuid "557ad879-3fe7-5cb0-b8c1-b0f06a41a395" 13194139534683 true] [17592186303238 1